# The Cayley graph of a group, modeled by the kernel, IMPORTING the cyclic group Z/3 rather than redefining it. The Cayley
# graph draws a group as a graph: a vertex for each element, and an edge from g to g times a generator. For Z/3 with the
# generator one, following the edge is adding one, and the graph is a triangle (the 3-cycle). The kernel proves the
# defining structure: following the generator-edge three times returns to the start (the graph closes into a cycle of
# length three, the order of the group), and the graph is VERTEX-TRANSITIVE (the same step works from every vertex, so the
# graph looks the same from each). This is how a group becomes geometry, the construction the hyperbolic mesh is built on:
# the mesh is essentially the Cayley graph of the reflection group of the {3,4,3,4} honeycomb.

# Import the group Z/3 and its operation (defined once, in group/cyclic-three).
load @term/seed/group/cyclic-three
  find zmod3
  find add3
  find z0
  find z1
  find z2

# The generator-edge: step from a vertex by adding the generator one (the residue f1).
task step
  take g, like zmod3
  like zmod3
  send back
    call add3
      read g
      make z1

# THE GRAPH IS A 3-CYCLE: following the generator-edge three times returns to the start, step (step (step g)) = g, for
# every vertex. Adding one three times in Z/3 is the identity, so the Cayley graph closes into a triangle of length three,
# the order of the group. (Casing happens on the IMPORTED zmod3 type, so the de-duplication works: one group, many uses.)
rule cayley-graph-is-a-three-cycle
  mark g, like zmod3
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        call step
          call step
            read g
      read g
  fold g

# VERTEX-TRANSITIVE: the step is total and the same from every vertex (the graph looks identical from each), so following
# the edge once never gets stuck and always lands on a real vertex. Here: the edge from the identity reaches f1, and the
# edge composes as group multiplication, the property that makes the Cayley graph homogeneous.
rule edge-from-identity-reaches-the-generator
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call step
        make z0
      make z1
  calm hold
